Subject: [PATCH] modeset: stop interlocked EVO submission on ring or notifier failure

Carry a sticky failure past the void HAL method emitters. Guard individual
data words, headers, reservation counts, wrap and kickoff. Do not invent a
notifier completion or rebuild a dead display channel to restore the console.
Use the owned per-open token for a host-only health query. Bound the RM
connector retry and its individual suggested sleeps. Mode and flip callers
must receive failure if the channel dies during their request.
The bounds are for polling while scheduled. They do not bound RM calls,
DMA completion, user file lifetime or acquisition of arbitrary kernel locks.

